# Vima Backend — Architecture & Conventions

Spring Boot 3.4.6 / Java / PostgreSQL / Flyway / Lombok

## Project Structure

```
src/main/java/com/vimainsurance/vimaadmin/
  controller/         — REST controllers (@RestController)
  service/            — Service interfaces (I*Service)
    serviceimpl/      — Service implementations (*ServiceImpl)
  entity/             — JPA entities (maps to DB tables)
  repository/         — Spring Data JPA repositories (I*Repository)
  dto/                — Data Transfer Objects (request/response)
  mapper/             — Static mapper classes (Entity ↔ DTO)
  enums/              — Enum types with getValue()/fromValue()
  config/             — Spring configuration (Security, CORS, etc.)
  exception/          — Custom exception classes
  util/               — Utility classes
  annotation/         — Custom annotations
  aspect/             — AOP aspects (rate limiting, etc.)
  security/           — Security-related classes
  scheduler/          — Scheduled tasks
  specification/      — JPA Specification builders

src/main/resources/
  application.properties          — Shared config + Flyway
  application-{profile}.properties — Profile-specific (dev, uat, prod)
  db/migration/                   — Flyway SQL migrations
  templates/email/                — Thymeleaf email templates
```

## Standard Response Wrapper

All endpoints return `ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<T>>`:

```java
public class ResponseDto<T> {
    private String message;
    private Integer errorCode = null;  // null on success
    private T payload;
    private long totalRecords = 0;
}

// Usage in service:
return ResponseEntity.ok(new ResponseDto<>("Success", data));
return ResponseEntity.ok(new ResponseDto<>("Success", data, totalRecords));
return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
    .body(new ResponseDto<>(400, "Validation failed"));
```

## Adding a New Feature (CRUD Pattern)

Reference: Endorsements (`/api/v1/batches`)

### Step 1 — Entity (`entity/*.java`)

```java
@Table(name = "endorsements", schema = "cpc")
@Getter @Setter @NoArgsConstructor @AllArgsConstructor @Data @Entity
public class Endorsement {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue
    @Column(name = "endorsement_id", columnDefinition = "UUID", updatable = false, nullable = false)
    private UUID endorsementId;

    @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
    @JoinColumn(name = "organization_id", nullable = false)
    private Organization organization;

    @Column(name = "status", nullable = false)
    @Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)
    @JdbcTypeCode(SqlTypes.NAMED_ENUM)
    private AccountStatus status = AccountStatus.PENDING_APPROVAL;

    @Column(name = "created_at", nullable = false, updatable = false)
    private LocalDateTime createdAt = LocalDateTime.now();

    @Column(name = "updated_at", nullable = false)
    private LocalDateTime updatedAt = LocalDateTime.now();
}
```

**Key conventions:**
- Schema: `cpc` for all business tables
- UUID primary keys with `@GeneratedValue`
- Lombok `@Getter @Setter @Data` (no manual getters/setters)
- `@JdbcTypeCode(SqlTypes.NAMED_ENUM)` for PostgreSQL enum columns
- `FetchType.LAZY` for all `@ManyToOne` relationships
- Default `createdAt`/`updatedAt` fields

### Step 2 — Repository (`repository/I*Repository.java`)

```java
@Repository
public interface IEndorsementRepository
    extends JpaRepository<Endorsement, UUID>, JpaSpecificationExecutor<Endorsement> {

    Optional<Endorsement> findByEndorsementId(UUID endorsementId);
    List<Endorsement> findByOrganization_OrganizationId(UUID organizationId);
    Page<Endorsement> findByStatus(AccountStatus status, Pageable pageable);

    // Custom JPQL queries when Spring Data naming isn't enough
    @Query("""
        SELECT e FROM Endorsement e
        WHERE e.organization.organizationId = :organizationId
        ORDER BY e.createdAt DESC
    """)
    List<Endorsement> findByOrganization(@Param("organizationId") UUID organizationId);

    // Native queries for aggregations
    @Query(value = """
        SELECT COUNT(e.endorsement_id) FROM cpc.endorsements e
        WHERE e.organization_id IN :orgIds
    """, nativeQuery = true)
    Long getCountByOrgs(@Param("orgIds") List<UUID> orgIds);
}
```

**Key conventions:**
- Extend both `JpaRepository<Entity, UUID>` and `JpaSpecificationExecutor<Entity>`
- Spring Data derived queries for simple cases
- `@Query` with JPQL for complex filtering
- `nativeQuery = true` for PostgreSQL-specific features

### Step 3 — DTOs (`dto/*.java`)

Request and Response DTOs are separate classes:

```java
// Request DTO — incoming from frontend
@Data
public class EndorsementRequestDto {
    @NotNull(message = "Organization ID is required")
    private UUID organizationId;
    private String endorsementType;
    private String status;
    private Integer totalEmployees;
}

// Response DTO — outgoing to frontend
@Data
public class EndorsementResponseDto {
    private UUID endorsementId;
    private UUID organizationId;
    private String organizationName;
    private String status;
    private LocalDateTime createdAt;
}
```

**Key conventions:**
- Lombok `@Data` for all DTOs
- `@NotNull` / `@NotBlank` / `@Email` from `jakarta.validation` for request DTOs
- Response DTOs flatten nested entity data (e.g., `organizationName` instead of nested object)
- Use `String` for enum fields in DTOs (not the enum type directly)
- Use `@Builder` when constructing DTOs in service layer

### Step 4 — Mapper (`mapper/*.java`)

Static utility class with three standard methods:

```java
public class EndorsementMapper {
    // Entity from Request DTO
    public static Endorsement mapToEntity(EndorsementRequestDto dto, Organization org) { ... }
    // Response DTO from Entity
    public static EndorsementResponseDto mapToResponseDto(Endorsement entity) { ... }
    // Update existing Entity from DTO (partial update)
    public static void updateEntityFromDto(Endorsement entity, EndorsementRequestDto dto) { ... }
}
```

**Key conventions:**
- All methods are `public static`
- Null-safe: check each field before mapping
- Enums: use `EnumType.fromValue(dto.getField())` when mapping from String
- Set `updatedAt = LocalDateTime.now()` on every mutation

### Step 5 — Service Interface + Impl

```java
// Interface
public interface IEndorsementService {
    ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<String>> create(EndorsementRequestDto requestDto);
    ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<EndorsementResponseDto>> getById(UUID endorsementId);
    ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<List<EndorsementResponseDto>>> getAllWithFilters(
        UUID organizationId, String status, int page, int size, String sortBy, String sortDirection);
}

// Implementation
@Service
public class EndorsementServiceImpl implements IEndorsementService {

    @Autowired
    private IEndorsementRepository endorsementRepository;

    @Autowired
    private IOrganizationRepository organizationRepository;

    @Override
    public ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<String>> create(EndorsementRequestDto dto) {
        // 1. Validate & fetch related entities
        // 2. Map DTO → Entity using Mapper
        // 3. Save via repository
        // 4. Return ResponseDto
    }
}
```

**Key conventions:**
- Interface naming: `I*Service`
- Impl in `serviceimpl/` subpackage
- `@Autowired` field injection for repositories (not constructor injection)
- Service returns `ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<T>>` directly
- Logging: `logger.info("[correlationId:{}] ...", MDC.get("correlationId"))`

### Step 6 — Controller

```java
@RestController
@CrossOrigin(allowedHeaders = "*")
@RequestMapping("/api/v1/batches")
public class EndorsementController {

    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(EndorsementController.class);

    @Autowired
    private IEndorsementService endorsementService;

    @PostMapping
    @PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ADMIN', 'VIMA_ADMIN')")
    public ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<String>> create(@RequestBody EndorsementRequestDto requestDto) {
        logger.info("[correlationId:{}] /endorsements (POST) endpoint called", MDC.get("correlationId"));
        return endorsementService.create(requestDto);
    }

    @GetMapping("/filtered")
    @PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ADMIN', 'VIMA_ADMIN', 'SALES_MANAGER', 'HR_ADMIN')")
    public ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<List<EndorsementResponseDto>>> getAllWithFilters(
            @RequestParam(required = false) UUID organizationId,
            @RequestParam(required = false) String status,
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page,
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "10") int size,
            @RequestParam(required = false) String sortBy,
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "desc") String sortDirection) {
        return endorsementService.getAllWithFilters(organizationId, status, page, size, sortBy, sortDirection);
    }

    // Multipart file upload
    @PostMapping(value = "/approve", consumes = MediaType.MULTIPART_FORM_DATA_VALUE)
    @PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ADMIN', 'VIMA_ADMIN')")
    public ResponseEntity<ResponseDto<String>> approve(
            @RequestPart(value = "files", required = false) MultipartFile[] files,
            @RequestPart("requestDto") EndorsementRequestDto requestDto) {
        return endorsementService.approve(files, requestDto);
    }
}
```

**Key conventions:**
- `@CrossOrigin(allowedHeaders = "*")` on all controllers
- `@RequestMapping("/api/v1/...")` — all paths start with `/api/v1/`
- `@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole(...)")` on every endpoint
- Log every endpoint entry with correlation ID
- Controllers are thin — delegate to service immediately
- Multipart: `@RequestPart` for JSON + file uploads

## Enum Pattern

```java
public enum EndorsementType {
    ADDITION("ADDITION"),
    DELETION("DELETION");

    private final String value;

    EndorsementType(String value) { this.value = value; }
    public String getValue() { return value; }

    public static EndorsementType fromValue(String value) {
        for (EndorsementType type : EndorsementType.values()) {
            if (type.value.equals(value)) return type;
        }
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unknown EndorsementType: " + value);
    }

    @Converter(autoApply = true)
    public static class EndorsementTypeConverter implements AttributeConverter<EndorsementType, String> {
        @Override public String convertToDatabaseColumn(EndorsementType t) { return t != null ? t.getValue() : null; }
        @Override public EndorsementType convertToEntityAttribute(String v) { return v != null ? fromValue(v) : null; }
    }
}
```

## Database

- **PostgreSQL** with schema `cpc` for all business tables
- **UUID** primary keys everywhere
- **JSONB** for flexible config/data (enrollment window config, submission data)
- **PostgreSQL enums** (`CREATE TYPE cpc.*_enum`) mapped with `@JdbcTypeCode(SqlTypes.NAMED_ENUM)`

## Flyway Migrations

Location: `src/main/resources/db/migration/`
Naming: `V{number}__{description}.sql` (double underscore)
Sub-versions: `V13.1__modify_tables.sql`

```sql
-- Example: V13__self_enrollment_create_tables.sql
CREATE TYPE cpc.endorsement_status_enum AS ENUM ('ACTIVE', 'SCHEDULED', ...);
CREATE TABLE cpc.enrollment_windows (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    organization_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES cpc.organizations(organization_id),
    status cpc.endorsement_status_enum NOT NULL DEFAULT 'SCHEDULED',
    config JSONB DEFAULT '{}',
    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

## User Roles & Personas

Roles defined in `enums/UserRole.java` (DB enum: `admin.user_role_enum`):

| Role | Backend Value | Frontend Value | Who | Access Level |
|------|--------------|----------------|-----|--------------|
| **Super Admin** | `SUPER_ADMIN` | — | System-level | Full system access, all operations |
| **Admin** | `ADMIN` | — | Legacy admin | Same as Super Admin (kept for backward compat) |
| **Vima Admin** | `VIMA_ADMIN` | `ROLE_VIMA_ADMIN` | Vima operations team | Manages all orgs, endorsements, enrollment windows, user management |
| **Sales Manager** | `SALES_MANAGER` | `ROLE_SALES_MANAGER` | Manages sales agents | Read access to endorsements, deals dashboard, org data |
| **Sales Agent** | `SALES_AGENT` | `ROLE_SALES_AGENT` | Sells policies | Deals, quotes, customer management |
| **HR Admin** | `HR_ADMIN` | `ROLE_HR_ADMIN` | Company HR personnel | Manages own org's enrollment windows, endorsements, employee data |
| **Employee** | — | `ROLE_EMPLOYEE` | Company employee | Self-service enrollment (token-based, no JWT login) |

### Access Control Matrix (Common Operations)

| Operation | SUPER_ADMIN | VIMA_ADMIN | SALES_MANAGER | HR_ADMIN | SALES_AGENT |
|-----------|:-----------:|:----------:|:-------------:|:--------:|:-----------:|
| Create/Update Endorsements | Yes | Yes | — | — | — |
| View Endorsements | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes (own org) | — |
| Approve Endorsements | Yes | Yes | — | — | — |
| Manage Enrollment Windows | Yes | Yes | — | Yes (own org) | — |
| Send Invitations/Reminders | Yes | Yes | — | Yes (own org) | — |
| View Enrollment Progress | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes (own org) | — |
| User Management | Yes | Yes | — | — | — |
| Feature Flags | Yes | Yes | — | — | — |

### How Roles Work

**Backend** — `@PreAuthorize` annotation on every controller method:
```java
// Vima Admin only (write operations)
@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ADMIN', 'VIMA_ADMIN')")

// Vima Admin + HR Admin (org-scoped read/write)
@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ADMIN', 'VIMA_ADMIN', 'HR_ADMIN')")

// Broad read access
@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ADMIN', 'VIMA_ADMIN', 'SALES_MANAGER', 'HR_ADMIN')")
```

**Frontend** — Zustand auth store + constant checks:
```typescript
import { useAuthStore } from "@/stores/useAuthStore";
import { USER_ROLES } from "@/constants";

const { userRole } = useAuthStore();
const isVimaAdmin = userRole === USER_ROLES.VIMA_ADMIN;
const isHRAdmin = userRole === USER_ROLES.HR_ADMIN;
// Conditionally render UI elements based on role
```

**Employee enrollment** uses token-based auth (no JWT login) — the `/api/v1/enrollment/**` endpoints are public and secured by magic link tokens instead.

### Tenant Isolation

HR Admins only see their own organization's data. This is enforced via:
1. `X-Organization-ID` header (set automatically by frontend interceptor)
2. `TenantFilter` in the Spring Security chain
3. Backend queries filter by `organizationId`

## Security

- **Authentik** OAuth2/OIDC for JWT validation in production
- **Dev profile** bypasses auth (mock user gets all roles)
- Public endpoints: `/health`, `/public/**`, `/api/v1/enrollment/**`
- Role-based access via `@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole(...)")`
- Tenant isolation via `X-Organization-ID` header + `TenantFilter`

## Key Dependencies

- **Lombok** — `@Data`, `@Builder`, `@Getter`, `@Setter` (no manual boilerplate)
- **Flyway** — Database migrations
- **Spring Security** — OAuth2 Resource Server + method security
- **Spring Data JPA** — Repositories + Specifications
- **Thymeleaf** — Email templates
- **AWS S3** — Document storage
- **OpenCSV / Apache POI** — CSV/Excel parsing
- **Bucket4j** — Rate limiting
- **Springdoc OpenAPI** — Swagger docs at `/swagger-ui.html`

## Profiles

- `dev` — Local development, auth bypassed, `server.servlet.context-path=/dev`
- `uat` — Staging, `server.servlet.context-path=/dev`, real auth
- `prod` — Production, `server.servlet.context-path=/prod`, real auth

Run with: `mvnd spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=uat`
